I reach the spice section.
I want black pepper.
There are many spices here.
I look at the shelves.
But I do not see black pepper.
I see a store assistant there.
I ask him.
"Excuse me, where is the black pepper?"
He smiles at me.
"It is on that shelf," he says.
He points out a specific packet.
"I like this brand," he says.
"This is very good black pepper."
"Thank you," I say to him.
I take that packet.
I put it in the cart.
